This extension adds Far Cry 5 modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]FC Mod Installer automatically installed.[/summary]

[b][size=3]This extension will automatically download and install the [/size][size=3][url=https://downloads.fcmodding.com/all/mod-installer/]FC Mod Installer[/url] for installing .a2/.a3/.a4/.a5/.bin files into the game files.[/size]
[url=https://mods.farcry.info/fc5][size=4]Click here to find FC Mod Installer Mods[/size][/url][/b]

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Epic[/*]
[*]Ubisoft Connect[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]FC Mod Installer installs to the "FCModInstaller" folder, recognised by a "fcmodinstaller.exe" file.[/*]
[*]Root Folder mods with a "bin" folder install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Game Data mods with a ".dat" file install to the "data_final\pc" folder.[/*]
[*]Binaries (Engine Injector) mods with a ".dll" file install to the "bin" folder.[/*]
[*]Repacked FCMI mods with an "info.xml" file install to the "FCModInstaller\ModifiedFilesFC5" folder.[/*]
[*]FCMI mods with a ".a2" file install to the "FCModInstaller\ModifiedFilesFC5" folder.[/*]
[*]XML Settings mods with a "gamerprofile.xml" file and a ".xml" file install to the "%USERPROFILE%\Documents\My Games\Far Cry 5\<User ID>" folder.[/*]
[*]Any other mod not described above installs to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Automatically installs Mod Installer to "FCModInstaller" folder.[/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Far Cry 5 mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Mod Installer (tool):

This installer handles the Far Cry Mod Installer, not mods for it. It exists so users can install the Far Cry Mod Installer through Vortex, and mod authors normally never package this.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a file named "fcmodinstaller.exe" in the archive.

  Installs to: "FCModInstaller"

  Common mistakes:
    - If you bundle the Far Cry Mod Installer inside your mod archive, Vortex treats the whole download as the Far Cry Mod Installer rather than as your mod. Ship the mod alone and list the Far Cry Mod Installer as a requirement.

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods laid out the same way the files appear inside the game folder. Vortex copies the matched folder and everything under it straight into the game.

[code]
MyRootMod.zip
└── bin\
    └── ... files in their real relative locations
[/code]

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a folder named "bin", "data_final" or "Support" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders, instead of the game folders themselves, adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

Data File Mods:

Packed game data replacements.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file with the ".dat" or ".fat" extensions.

  Installs to: "data_final\pc"

========================================================================

Binaries (Engine Injector):

Recognised when the archive contains a ".dll" file.

  Installs to: "bin"

========================================================================

Repacked FCMI Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a "info.xml" file.

  Installs to: "FCModInstaller\ModifiedFilesFC5"

========================================================================

Mod Installer Mods:

Mods packaged for the Far Cry Mod Installer.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file with the ".a2", ".a3", ".a4", ".a5" or ".bin" extensions.

  Installs to: "FCModInstaller\ModifiedFilesFC5"

  Common mistakes:
    - These are applied through the Mod Installer tool, not deployed straight into the game.

========================================================================

XML Settings Mod:

Recognised when the archive contains a "gamerprofile.xml" file and a ".xml" file.

  Installs to: "%USERPROFILE%\Documents\My Games\Far Cry 5\<User ID>"

========================================================================

Fallback Installer:

The catch-all. Any archive that matched none of the installers above lands here and is copied across unchanged.

[b][color=#ffff00]NOTE: Landing in the fallback installer is a signal your archive layout needs fixing.[/color][/b]

  Requirements:
    - Reaching this installer usually means the archive was not laid out in a way Vortex recognised.
    - Vortex shows the user a notification when a mod installs through the fallback.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - If your mod lands here unintentionally, re-check the layouts above - users will see a fallback warning and may report the mod as broken.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]

